{
 "id": "openqasm",
 "name": "OpenQASM",
 "aliases": ["Open Quantum Assembly Language", "QASM", "OpenQASM 3"],
 "categories": ["quantum", "assembly", "intermediate-representation"],
 "paradigms": ["imperative", "circuit-description"],
 "typing": ["static"],
 "first_appeared": 2017,
 "designers": ["Andrew W. Cross", "Lev S. Bishop", "John A. Smolin", "Jay M. Gambetta", "Ali Javadi-Abhari", "Blake R. Johnson"],
 "summary": "Imperative quantum assembly / circuit-description language originating at IBM: OpenQASM 2 describes gate-level circuits on qubit registers, while OpenQASM 3 adds classical control flow, typed classical data, subroutines, timing (duration/stretch/delay/box) and pulse-level calibrations via OpenPulse.",
 "status": "active",
 "defined_by": ["community-specification", "academic-paper"],
 "file_extensions": [".qasm"],
 "homepage": "https://openqasm.com/",
 "related": [{"id": "quantum-circuit-model", "relation": "formalizes"}, {"id": "qir", "relation": "family"}, {"id": "quil", "relation": "family"}],
 "level_notes": {"1": "The live specification at openqasm.com (maintained by the OpenQASM Technical Steering Committee, with versioned 3.0/3.1 snapshots and an ANTLR grammar) defines OpenQASM 3; OpenQASM 2 is defined by the 2017 arXiv paper. The 2022 ACM TQC paper is the defining paper for v3. No official formal semantics; SQIR/VOQC give a verified semantics for the OpenQASM 2 gate subset.", "0": "The openqasm/openqasm repo holds the grammar and the reference Python AST/parser (openqasm3 package). Production parsers live in Qiskit (Rust qasm2/qasm3 crates), qe-qasm (C++) and many SDKs (Braket, pytket, etc.)."},
